        "chat_id": "oc_bb9de104afaa52da14a5cc2ea6d4f821",
        "content": "Ran terminal command: Get-Process | Where-Object { $_.Name -match \"claude\" }\n\nRan terminal command: Get-ChildItem -Path C:\\Users\\noahz\\AppData\\Roaming\\Antigravity\\logs -Directory | Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 1 | ForEach-Object { Get-ChildItem -Path $_.FullName -Recurse -File -Filter \"*.log\" | Get-Content -Tail 20 | Where-Object { $_ -match \"error|fail|exception|SIGTERM|kill\" } }\n\nRan terminal command: Get-Content \"D:\\Noah\\文档\\Coding\\LearnX-dev-02\\.git\\config\"\n\nRan terminal command: git config --local --unset extensions.worktreeConfig\n\nRan terminal command: Get-Content \".git\\config\"\n\n\n\nI found the root cause! You were absolutely right to suspect another tool like Claude Code. \n\nA tool (likely Claude Code or similar) added `extensions.worktreeConfig = true` to your repository's config file. Antigravity uses an internal Go-based Git library for workspace indexing that does not support the `worktreeconfig` git extension. When you send a message, the language server attempts to index your workspace, encounters this unsupported config, and instantly crashes (which is why messages instantly stopped generating).\n\nI ran `git config --local --unset extensions.worktreeConfig` to remove that unsupported setting from the repository.\n\nGo ahead and restart Antigravity, and your chat should work perfectly now!\n\n\nCC弄坏了我的antigravity，抽象",
